# Honeywell V200HL ALT Analyzer

## Project Overview

### Purpose

Build a lightweight local-first analytics application that automates analysis of Honeywell V200HL Accelerated Life Test (ALT) logs.

The tool replaces manual decoding of EEPROM data dumps and manual report creation.

Target users:

* Internal engineering interns
* Test engineers
* Validation engineers

Deployment target:

* Local machine only
* No cloud
* No authentication
* No database
* No enterprise features

Primary objective:

Convert raw ALT log files into structured analytics and reports within seconds.

---

# Core Design Principles

## Principle 1: Local First

Everything runs locally.

No external APIs.

No cloud storage.

No internet dependency.

No telemetry.

No account system.

---

## Principle 2: Extremely Lightweight

Preferred stack:

* Python 3.11+
* Streamlit
* Pandas
* Plotly
* NumPy

Avoid:

* React
* NextJS
* FastAPI
* Django
* PostgreSQL
* MongoDB
* Redis
* Docker

Unless a future requirement absolutely demands them.

---

## Principle 3: Deterministic Parsing

Never infer protocol structure.

Parser must use explicit byte offsets.

Every decoded field must be traceable back to source bytes.

---

## Principle 4: Separation of Concerns

The project must be separated into:

* Parsing
* Validation
* Analysis
* Visualization
* Reporting

No module should mix responsibilities.

